r hall. This quaint barn-looking building was built in the mid-16th century and was used by the Butcher Corporation.\" data-attachment-id=\"5288\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"Today&#039;s Tourism Office is located in the old butcher hall. This quaint barn-looking building was built in the mid-16th century and was used by the Butcher Corporation.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2020\/03\/20181229_134349\/4003138177.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Today's Tourism Office is located in the old butcher hall. This quaint barn-looking building was built in the mid-16th century and was used by the Butcher Corporation.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/20181229_134319.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Don&#039;t hesitate to enter the Tourism Office. The representatives will be happy to assist you :)\" data-attachment-id=\"5289\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"Don&#039;t hesitate to enter the Tourism Office. The representatives will be happy to assist you :)\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2020\/03\/20181229_134319\/4262985619.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Don't hesitate to enter the Tourism Office. The representatives will be happy to assist you \ud83d\ude42<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/20181229_134717.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Located on the Quay Street, right next to the Tourism Office, the building to the left with the protruding upper floors is one of the oldest remaining buildings of the city. Built in the 16th century, it underwent some renovations in the 17th century.\n&lt;p&gt;More importantly though, if you are a fan of farmers markets, be sure to come back to this Quay Street as it is closed to cars every Sunday to make way for the Sunday Market that stretches all along this street. Some call it the largest market in Belgium.&lt;\/p&gt;\" data-attachment-id=\"5287\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"Located on the Quay Street, right next to the Tourism Office, the building to the left with the protruding upper floors is one of the oldest remaining buildings of the city. Built in the 16th century, it underwent some renovations in the 17th century.\n&lt;p&gt;More importantly though, if you are a fan of farmers markets, be sure to come back to this Quay Street as it is closed to cars every Sunday to make way for the Sunday Market that stretches all along this street. Some call it the largest market in Belgium.&lt;\/p&gt;\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2020\/03\/20181229_134717\/1477468799.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Located on the Quay Street, right next to the Tourism Office, the building to the left with the protruding upper floors is one of the oldest remaining buildings of the city. Built in the 16th century, it underwent some renovations in the 17th century.\n<p>More importantly though, if you are a fan of farmers markets, be sure to come back to this Quay Street as it is closed to cars every Sunday to make way for the Sunday Market that stretches all along this street. Some call it the largest market in Belgium.<\/p><\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/03\/20181229_135950.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Built in 1738, this building came to be known as the Hotel Ansembourg in reference to the family that occupied the residence over 60 years. Today, it is the Ansembourg Museum, showcasing regional furniture pieces during the Enlightenment.\" data-attachment-id=\"5286\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"Built in 1738, this building came to be known as the Hotel Ansembourg in reference to the family that occupied the residence over 60 years. Today, it is the Ansembourg Museum, showcasing regional furniture pieces during the Enlightenment.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/iboishin.github.io/portfolio-website\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2020\/03\/20181229_135950\/2321900868.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22ht